---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RecipeCard from '../components/RecipeCard.astro';
import Ornament from '../components/Ornament.astro';
import gooseMedallion from '../assets/brand/source/goose-medallion.webp';
import { getRecipes, showFixtures } from '../lib/content';
const recipes = await getRecipes();
const featured = recipes.slice(0, 3);
---
<BaseLayout title="The Tipsy Goose" description="A playful home cooking and cocktail publication about making dinner more personal, capable, and fun—with honest help from generative AI.">
  {showFixtures && <div class="fixture-ribbon">Development preview · fixture content is visible and will not ship</div>}
  <section class="page-masthead">
    <div class="shell grid items-center gap-8 py-12 md:py-16 lg:grid-cols-[1.08fr_.72fr] lg:gap-14 lg:py-20">
      <div class="relative z-10 py-3 lg:py-8">
        <p class="eyebrow text-brass-bright">Dinner should have a plot twist.</p>
        <div class="mt-10">
          <h1 class="display max-w-3xl">A little less meal kit.<br/><em class="text-brass-bright">A lot more you.</em></h1>
          <p class="mt-9 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-cream/78">The Tipsy Goose turns grocery-store ingredients, personal taste, and a well-aimed prompt into dinners worth lingering over. The ideas may start with AI. The judgment happens at the stove.</p>
          <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a href="/recipes" class="button border-cream text-cream">Browse the recipe book</a><a href="/about" class="button border-cream/30 text-cream">How this works</a></div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-11 max-w-xl border-l border-brass pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-cream/65">No mystery subscription box. No claim that an untested idea is a finished recipe. Just a better way to plan, learn, cook, revise—and pour something civilized.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-[31rem] self-center lg:justify-self-end">
        <div class="absolute inset-4 rounded-[50%] border border-brass/40" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <Image src={gooseMedallion} alt="An engraved white goose in a burgundy waistcoat and bow tie holding a martini, framed by an antique brass oval" width={627} height={627} priority class="relative block h-auto w-full object-contain drop-shadow-[0_24px_35px_rgba(0,0,0,.35)]" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell py-20 lg:py-24">
    <Ornament class="mb-10 text-brass" />
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.85fr_1.15fr] lg:gap-24">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The proposition</p><h2 class="section-title mt-5">Convenience without surrendering dinner.</h2></div>
      <div class="grid gap-8 text-base leading-7 text-ink/75 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <p>Meal kits make decisions disappear. Useful, sometimes. But ordinary grocery stores plus a flexible plan can do more: match your appetite, use the half-bunch of parsley, teach a technique, and change when Tuesday goes sideways.</p>
        <p>Generative AI helps sketch the possibilities and organize the work. Human taste decides what sounds good. Real cooking decides what survives publication. Every recipe tells you where it stands.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="double-rule bg-paper py-20 lg:py-24">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-6"><div><p class="eyebrow">From the kitchen</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4">Recipes with receipts.</h2></div><a href="/recipes" class="button">Open the archive</a></div>
      {featured.length ? <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">{featured.map(recipe => <RecipeCard recipe={recipe} />)}</div> : <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="paper-panel p-6 md:col-span-2 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">Prelaunch</p><Ornament class="mt-8 text-brass" compact /><p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl font-display text-4xl leading-[1] tracking-[-.025em] sm:text-5xl">The pans are hot. The archive is not pretending to be full.</p><p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-ink/65">The first recipes will arrive with clear testing status, structured ingredients, useful timing, and notes on what changed in the kitchen.</p></div>
        <div class="border border-brass bg-green p-6 text-cream sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow text-brass-bright">What you’ll find</p><ul class="mt-12 space-y-5 font-display text-2xl"><li>Food & cocktails</li><li>Complete dinner menus</li><li>Technique notes</li><li>Honest experiments</li></ul></div>
      </div>}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">The working method</p>
    <div class="mt-7 grid border-y border-green/20 md:grid-cols-4">
      {['Start with a real appetite', 'Ask for useful possibilities', 'Cook, notice, and adjust', 'Publish what we actually know'].map((item, i) => <div class="border-green/20 px-5 py-8 md:border-l first:md:border-l-0"><span class="font-display text-5xl text-brass">0{i + 1}</span><h3 class="mt-10 text-3xl">{item}</h3></div>)}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
